I, Lukko the Elven Priest, was exploring the Mines, and things were
going quite well.  A wish was used to get some nice dragon skin armor,
and I was fast as well.

I encountered a strange level, with tunnels and pits dug all around.
Two cats (both named Snertkat) bounded over to greet me.  Continuing
onward, I found a grave, and read the inscription, "Kroisos, killed by
a tiger, while helpless"

A tiger!  Oh no!  I'm not ready to fight a tiger.  Hmm... but where is
it?  Meow?

Very strange, but it's not here.

Oh well.  I wandered along a bit further, and... what's this?  Another
grave.  Peering into the darkness I read, "Kroisos, choked on a tiger
corpse"

I couldn't help but laugh aloud at my doubly good fortune.  Thanks (and
more thanks) to Kroisos.


